   "title": "CMTI test circuit",
   "page": 14,
   "fixture": true,
   "description": "The fixture for common-mode transient immunity. A switch puts IN+ at VDD or at GND while IN- stays grounded, so the output is held high or low. A pulse generator between the logic ground and GNDISO slews the whole isolated side against the input side, and the joined GON and GOFF pins are watched for a wrong state during the slew. VH comes from a source across a bypass capacitor.",
